# --- Destination image library (flyg.ai import) ---
# Everything under public/images/destinations is tracked, heroes AND thumbnails.
#
# DO NOT IGNORE THE THUMBNAILS AGAIN. They used to be ignored on the grounds that
# they were "unused in code". That stopped being true when the warm guide was
# built, and the rule outlived the fact: app/lib/climate.ts, WarmSearch.tsx and
# where-is-it-warm/page.tsx all render `d.thumbnail`, which is 541 distinct
# thumbnails across the built site.
#
# The failure mode is why this comment is long. Ignoring them breaks 535 image
# paths in production and NOTHING CATCHES IT: the files sit on the developer's
# disk, so every local build succeeds, next build reports no error, and the
# broken images only appear once Vercel builds from a clean checkout. It looked
# correct in dev the whole way through.
#
# The cost of tracking them is about 8 MB against the 68 MB the folder already
# holds. The alternative — pointing the cards at the full-size `image` instead —
# would make every card roughly ten times heavier on pages that render 130 of
# them, which undoes the image-weight work in PERFORMANCE.md.

.vercel
.env*.local

# Local scratch/backup dirs — never commit
scratchpad/
scripts/.fare-months-progress
scripts/.direct-progress
